{
  "title": "THA Vascular Injury & Bleeding",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/recon/422741/tha-vascular-injury-and-bleeding",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Aug 31 2023",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "THA Vascular Injury and Bleeding is a rare, potentially devastating, complication during total hip arthroplasty that may occur as a result of errant retractor placement, acetabular screw placement, or direct laceration of a vessel during the surgical approach.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with visual inspection for significant arterial bleeding and a change in patient hemodynamic status.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is prompt recognization of the injured vessel, hemostasis and vascular consultation.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "0.1%-0.2%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "acetabular screw placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "prior vascular bypass or dysvascuar limb",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "revision arthroplasty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "intra-pelvic position of acetabular component and femoral cerclage wiring",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "mechanism of Injury",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "puncture or laceration from acetabular screw placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "errant retractor placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "placement of inferior retractor under the **transverse acetabular ligament places the obturator artery** at risk.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "compression by anti-protrusio acetabular components",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "direct laceration during approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Medial femoral circumflex artery",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "underneath the gluteus maximus tendon and/or quadratus femoris muscle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Obturator artery and vein",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "distal to the transverse acetabular ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ascending branch of the lateral femoral circumflex artery",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "ascends between tensor fasciae latae and sartorius",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "encountered during direct anterior approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "External iliac vessels",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "lie 7mm away from bone at level of ASIS",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "reports of vessels lying immediately adjacent bone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Common femoral vessels",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "lie superficial to iliopsoas",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "separated from hip by only anterior capsule and iliopsoas",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Quadrants of acetabulum",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422741/images/tab_quadrants_miller..jpg",
              "caption": "Diagram of acetabular quadrants for screw placement"
            }
